### Base URL — change to http://noteshare-sharing:8083 when testing inside Docker
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8083

### JWT from auth service — run auth.http step 4 first to populate this
@jwt = {{jwt_token}}


### ─── HAPPY PATH ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 1. Create a note first (in notes service) — get a noteId to share
### Run notes.http step 1 first, then set note_id here:
@noteId = {{note_id}}


### 2. Create a share link — expect 201; token saved to share_token variable
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/share/{{noteId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}

> {%
    client.global.set("share_token", response.body.token);
    client.test("Create share returns 201", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "Expected 201");
        client.assert(response.body.token !== undefined, "Expected token in body");
    });
%}


### 3. Resolve share link — no auth required, returns full note content
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/share/{{share_token}}


### ─── ERROR CASES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 4. Resolve with unknown token — expect 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/share/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000


### 5. Create share without token — expect 401 or 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/share/{{noteId}}
